{
  "case_id": "2020-19-897",
  "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Vivek Suri (Petitioners' counsel)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents are detained under Section 1231, not under Section 1226. In the first place, the text of Section 1231 refers repeatedly to an order of removal or to the aliens who have been ordered removed. That is clear from the caption, from the operative provision, and from the definition of the removal period. There is no dispute here that these aliens have been ordered removed. Indeed, that is the definition of reinstating a removal order."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, Mr. Suri, if an alien is in withholding-only proceedings and there's no country other than the one, you know, as to which he claims statutory withholding or CAT relief, can you remove him?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "briefly how the district court had jurisdiction under 1252 in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Vivek Suri (Petitioners' counsel)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The best answer I have is this Court's decision last term in Nasrallah, where the Court said that a removal order's finality is not affected by CAT protection. And it doesn't matter whether 10 percent or 20 percent or some other percentage do or don't ultimately leave the country."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Vivek Suri (Petitioners' counsel)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The supervised release conditions are set out in Section 1231(a)(3). It provides, for example, that the alien must appear before an immigration officer periodically for identification, must submit, if necessary, to a medical examination, and must obey written restrictions on the alien's conduct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. Suri. I wanted to ask about a passage in your reply brief on pages 12 and 13. Your argument, as I understand it, is, under 1231, that there is a final order of removal dating back to the original order of removal. But, for purposes of 1252, the question becomes, is there some chance for judicial review of -- of the withholding-only proceedings?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, since you asked me to take a position, yes, the government's position is that review would be available and that \"final\" would have to mean something different in 1252."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. Suri. In the Fourth Circuit's opinion by Judge Harris, the opinions offered a contextual argument, page 877, \"The fact that the removal period is limited to 90 days strongly suggests that it is intended to apply only when all legal barriers to removal are cleared away,\" in other words, using the fact of the 90-day limit to help interpret these two provisions together. What's your response to that argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BARRETT",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, I have a question about the post-order custody review. Once the removal period ends once you hit that 90-day mark, do the regulations that govern the post-order custody review automatically kick in so that the detained noncitizen gets some sort of hearing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: In Nasrallah versus Barr, you were successful. And I wonder how you can reconcile the argument that the Court accepted there about administrative finality"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hughes",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "our first argument to start is the gateway provision of (a)(1)(A), which is to say it defines and limits the removal period as the time that the government can actually execute on the removal order."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let me ask you -- let me squeeze in one more question. To what degree is your argument dependent on the statistics that were discussed earlier about the feasibility of removal to a third country?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, how much of your argument depends on your due process concern? As I understood, one of your arguments in your brief is, if we read it the government's way, we're inviting the potential of due process violations. Is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hughes",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "it's exactly the arguments that this Court in Zadvydas adopted, which is to say there's no neutral arbitrator."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-897",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f19b7e17b04e7cdedc4943e01c8a0f15ef697b7c638a50382c3742c2dada76fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f19b7e17b04e-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
